1.8.10-snapshot
  Dynamic jobs, attachments across the stalker economy, and longer loot claims
    Flavor is a new tab. A calm stalker near you takes a short job where he stands, picked by his situation, then returns to his routine.
    Trade, Barter, Loot policy and Stash Fill now handle attachments. Stalkers keep, buy, barter and stash the scopes, silencers and launchers that fit their guns, and a trade visit is capped.
    Other things you will notice. Loot claims reach sniping distance, the overheard loot lines have a chance slider, companions hold no claim, and A-Life runs faster near anomalies.

  Economy
    Loot claim
      - Changed the claim ranges to a stalker's sight range. If you kill a man at sniping distance, the body stays yours while you walk to it with a clear line to it.
      - Added a chance slider for the lines you overhear when a stalker leaves your kill, and 0 silences them. The warning when you reach for an NPC's kill stays.
      - Fixed killing your own companion reserving his body as your kill, which kept stalkers from looting it.
      - Fixed a companion holding a kill against you right after a load.
      - Fixed a reload restarting every claim. A claim now ends a fixed time after the kill, and a save from 1.8.9 or older clears its old claims once.
    Loot policy
      - Changed a looting stalker to keep up to 2 loose attachments, plus one that fits his pistol and one that fits his rifle. Each one counted as a spare gun before.
    Trade
      - Changed trade to let a stalker keep up to 2 loose attachments. He sold every attachment as a spare weapon before.
      - Added Max items bought per trade. A stalker restocks in policy order with ammo first, and when he arrives empty he tops up over several visits.
        A trade used to spawn as much as his money could buy.
      - Added attachment buying. A veteran buys the cheapest attachment that fits his pistol or rifle, one per gun on each visit.
        A silencer or launcher goes onto the gun, and a scope stays in his pack. A rookie keeps one that fits but never buys one.
    Barter
      - Changed barter to hand ammo and attachments only to a stalker whose gun takes them. A spare scope or silencer now reaches a peer whose gun fits it.
        Barter used to hand over ammo the other stalker's gun could not fire, and the inventory cleanup deleted it.

  News
    - Fixed News logging an engine error when vanilla's list of online stalkers kept an id the game had reused for an artefact.

  Consequences
    Stash Fill
      - Changed a squad filling a stash to keep up to 2 loose attachments and deposit the rest.

  Flavor
    Dynamic jobs
      - Added Dynamic jobs. A calm stalker near you takes a short job where he stands, a smoke, a drink, the PDA or binoculars, then returns to his routine.
        Vanilla hands out jobs only through smart terrain slots. Here any stalker qualifies, in camp, on patrol or walking past, and his situation picks the job.
        Near an artefact anomaly he sweeps a detector, and when a mutant is close he turns wary. A squad leader gives orders, the military factions drill and bandits sway drunk.
        An enemy or a danger ends the job at once.

  Performance
    - Improved A-Life performance near anomalies.

  Development
    - Changed the world trace roster to name each controlled squad's section.

1.8.9
  Trader stock that follows NPC trading, overheard stalkers, and a chase crash fix
    The Market now reads both sides of NPC trading. A trader's shelf thins by how much his faction's stalkers buy, each type by a different amount at each restock.
    Added economy chatter. You overhear stalkers near you resupplying, selling a haul or stripping a body, and AlifePlus reports read as part of the vanilla PDA feed.
    Other things you will notice. Each report speaks in a different voice, and a rare chase crash is gone.

  Economy
    Market
      - Changed the sell-out to follow how much a faction's stalkers buy. Each type they go through runs short by a different amount every restock, and a quiet faction keeps full shelves.
      - Changed the sell-out to reach every supply stalkers buy, grenades, food, drink and crafting parts included.
      - Changed the default stock per trader upward, and the shelf turns over faster between your visits.

  News
    - Added overheard chatter. A stalker near you says that he resupplied or sold a haul at a trader, passed a gun to a squadmate or stripped a body.
    - Changed AlifePlus reports to share the vanilla PDA feed. A report from any channel, ours or vanilla, holds the next line back for a moment.
    - Changed every report and chatter pool to vary its voice, and the chatter names only notable items.

  General
    - Fixed a rare crash when X-Ray gave a dead squad's id to another object while a chase against that squad was still tracked.

1.8.8
  The loot claim rework, outpost service removal, and the world trace
    The loot claim of 1.8.0 now needs a clear line to the body wherever you are involved, and nobody claims a corpse through a wall.
    Turning off Grow services now clears the outposts already placed, and the world trace dumps the squads AlifePlus controls.

  Territory
    Conquest
      - Changed Grow services so that turning it off removes the outpost services already placed on the next load. Guards and area ownership stay.

  Economy
    Loot claim
      - Changed kill reservation to need a clear line to the body wherever you are involved, as well as distance. Designed with Bazinga and John.Sick.
        An owner blocks you only while he can see the body, and an NPC leaves your kill only while you can see it. Between NPCs, distance alone still holds.
      - Added separate range sliders for the reserve, the block and the NPC-vs-NPC claim.
      - Changed the loot claim lines to follow the same rule as the claim. The hands-off warning fires when you try to loot.
        Rarer overheard lines cover an NPC leaving your kill or passing up another squad's.

  Development
    - Changed the world trace log to dump the squads AlifePlus controls with their dispatch record, every squad, NPC and mutant on the level, and where squads pile up on a smart.
      Each line carries the character name, so a stalker from a screenshot or a clip can be found in the log.

1.8.7
  Outpost mini bases, population-driven conquest, and off-map destinations by drive
    Conquest outposts now hold service NPCs and a guard detail. They man a conquered area, kept manned by the vanilla respawn while the area is held.
    Conquest now follows the level's population. A weak faction takes more ground and a dominant one less, and mutants swarm and nest by the same rule.
    Other things you will notice. Each off-map drive heads to a different kind of place, loot lines need a close look at the body, and a level change loads faster.

  Territory
    Conquest
      - Changed a held area to grow service NPCs and a guard detail from the vanilla respawn rows and jobs. The old outpost scripted the NPCs and swapped their models by hand.
      - Changed conquest to follow the level's population. A weak faction conquers more and a dominant one less, each up to a set number of areas, and mutants swarm and nest the same way.
      - Added a money limit for outpost services that resets at each restock. Selling them loot runs it out until the next one.
      - Changed outpost services to spawn as ordinary faction NPCs with a shop, a map icon and a job at the area. Trader stock mods recognize them.
      - Changed decay to undo the outpost. Each service becomes an ordinary stalker, the guards stay as ordinary squads, and the area returns to its LTX spawns.
      - Changed the Area respawn sliders of Conquest, Swarm and Infest to refill a held area under its squad count when the world respawn is slower.
        It works under GAMMA and vanilla, spawns out of your view, and runs no faster than the world would.
      - Removed the outpost model dressing. A service wears the look of his profile.
      - Changed the first load of an older save to remove its outpost services, squadless leftovers included, and the held areas build a fresh base.
      - Fixed a crash when a held outpost respawned a service squad whose section was missing. The spawn is skipped. Reported by JossieDiaz.

  Economy
    Loot claim
      - Fixed loot claim lines from a stalker too far from the kill to see it. A stalker speaks only when he is close to both the body and the one he addresses, and can see each. Reported by Bazinga.
    Trade
      - Changed trade, barter, stash fill and loot to let a stalker keep an armour plate. He used to sell or deposit every plate he carried.

  Needs
    - Changed off-map travel so each drive heads to its own kind of place, a supply run to a faction base, a barter run to an occupied field camp and a social visit to a campfire.

  Development
    - Added Flush log every line, which writes each log line to disk at once, so a crash keeps its last lines for a bug report.
    - Added World trace log, periodic dumps of smarts, squads, the controlled squads and trader inventories to a separate alifeplus_world.log.
    - Fixed the PDA marker of a squad chasing another squad fading in the middle of the chase.

  Performance
    - Improved level change and save load performance. The framework holds less state and does less work on each load.
    - Improved A-Life tracing performance. The default log level allocates no tracing memory.

1.8.6
  Outpost service roles, shelves, posts and looks, and kept artefacts
    An outpost service now trades, repairs or heals from a shelf for his role, at a post around the area center.
    Each service wears a look from his faction's wardrobe, carries a sidearm and spawns at the rank of a faction regular.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers keep an artefact, binoculars and a night vision device, and trader stock addons reach every outpost service.

  Territory
    Conquest
      - Changed an outpost service to trade, repair or heal only. A mission taken before this change can still be turned in.
      - Changed outpost stock to a cap per category, and ammo to a cap per type in rounds. An outpost trader deals mainly in ammunition. Reported by Charles Peugeot.
      - Changed each service role to stock from a list of its kind. A barman keeps a full pantry, a medic a full dispensary and a mechanic his tools and detectors.
      - Added a post and a PDA icon for every barman, mechanic and medic, as the trader has.
      - Changed a service that is hijacked, displaced or loses his job to return to his post, or to be replaced when he cannot, instead of wandering off or trailing you.
      - Changed outpost services to stand at separate points around the area center, each facing in. Reported by Charles Peugeot.
      - Added a look from the faction's wardrobe for each service, a different one for each service of a faction on a map. Renegades wear bandit masks. Reported by Charles Peugeot.
      - Added a sidearm for each outpost service. Reported by jacksob.
      - Changed an outpost service to spawn at a regular rank. Killing one hits faction relations like any ordinary kill.
      - Changed trader stock addons to recognize every outpost service. Destockifiers and injectors reach area barmen, mechanics and medics. Reported by Charles Peugeot.
      - Changed the areas of an older save to reset to 1 service on the first load and grow again. Reported by Charles Peugeot.

  Economy
    - Fixed stalkers selling, bartering and looting away their artefacts, binoculars and night vision devices until they carried none.
      A stalker now keeps one of each and moves only the surplus, and those items turn up on the bodies you loot again.

1.8.5
  The outpost trader at his post, a field stock below the hub, and service variety
    The outpost trader now holds his post, stocks a lean field assortment below his faction's hub, and restocks through the game's trader pipeline.
    Held areas now grow a mix of services, the least common role first, and a map gets traders, barmen, mechanics and medics.
    Other things you will notice. A killed service drops only a stalker's loot, the trader has a PDA icon, and areas decay later by default.

  Territory
    Conquest
      - Fixed the outpost trader leaving his post to follow you around the level. Reported by Rambito.
      - Changed a killed service NPC to drop only the loot of a stalker of his rank. He used to drop his whole shop stock. Suggested by Derda.
      - Changed a held area to grow 1 service, the role a faction's areas have least, tuned by Max services per level and Max same service per faction per level.
      - Added the PDA trader icon for the outpost trader, shown like a hub trader's and hidden while his faction is hostile to you.
      - Changed the outpost trader to stock below his faction's hub trader. His stock follows your goodwill and wealth, then drops a set number of tiers. Reported by Greshnik5126.
      - Added a lean field stock for outpost services, set in a DLTX config. It sells ammo, medical, provisions, a few grenades and repair parts, and leaves out weapons and armor. Suggested by BigPok.
      - Changed the outpost trader to restock through the game's trader pipeline. Trader stock addons govern him like any trader.
      - Changed the default decay of a conquered area to a longer one, and the service NPC now goes with the area.

1.8.4
  Alpha combat, territory takeovers, outpost services and NPC barter
    Creatures is a new tab, and the alpha combat cut in 1.7.0 returns. Each kill makes an alpha hit harder and take less, and it carries trophy parts and a dust shimmer.
    Conquest, swarms and infestations become takeovers. The holder owns the area until its claim decays, and a held camp grows outpost services.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers barter within their faction, companions can loot your kills, and squads gather at campfires across the map.

  Territory
    Conquest
      - Added outpost services on held camps. A trader takes a post at the camp center and works as a full shopkeeper, alongside a barman, a mechanic or a medic who trade, repair and heal.
        Guards and residents keep their patrols and camp jobs around them, and every service stocks the faction's market.
      - Changed conquest to a takeover. The winning faction owns the area, which respawns only its squads and refills faster while held, capped by the map's danger tier.
        A held area stays locked until its claim decays, and wiping the holders leaves it with them.
    Swarm
      - Added mutant swarms. Pack and lair species, bloodsuckers, snorks, dogs and cats, take an empty smart the way stalkers conquer, and it respawns only their species while held.
        Solo bosses and vermin never take ground.
    Infest
      - Added infestations. A pack with an alpha turns a den into a nest that holds more squads than a swarm and replaces the smart's spawns until it decays.

  Creatures
    Alpha
      - Added alpha combat. Each alpha level raises the damage an alpha deals and lowers the damage it takes, with separate caps against you and against NPCs.
        An alpha never panics, and its corpse carries the species hide and extra trophy parts.
      - Added a dust shimmer on every alpha's body. You can tell the pack leader on sight.

  Economy
    Loot claim
      - Added a toggle that lets your companions loot the bodies you killed. They stay off your kills by default, like any NPC.
    Barter
      - Added NPC barter. A supply-short squad at a friendly smart swaps surplus for what it lacks with a stalker of its faction, and no money changes hands.
        Ammo for its guns, medical supplies, grenades, and a weapon, outfit or helmet that beats what the other carries move. An off-map version travels to a friendly squad on another map.

  Needs
    - Changed campfire detection to cover the whole map. Squads gather at fires everywhere, where they used to gather only in bases or near you.

1.8.3
  The market sell-out, trader chatter, better NPC restocks and presence-capped conquest
    The Market now works both ways, and a trader runs short of the staples his faction's stalkers keep buying.
    Trade restocks more. Stalkers restock usable ammo, food, drink and anti-rad, and conquest follows a faction's live presence on a level.
    Other things you will notice. A stalker remarks when a trader runs short, off-map squads release their members, and the MCM resets speak Russian.

  Territory
    - Changed conquest and swarming to read a faction's live presence on a level. A faction with nothing on a level always gets its first area, and dominant factions stop while newcomers expand.
      The old rule favoured the dominant faction.
    - Changed the last smart a community holds on a level to stay out of conquest, swarm and infestation, so no faction is wiped off a map.
    - Changed the Max conquered and Max swarmed per level sliders to Max faction smarts per level under Causes > Opportunities, one for conquest and one for swarm.

  Economy
    Market
      - Added the sell-out. A trader's stock of the staples his faction's stalkers keep buying shrinks at each restock. A faction that trades heavily leaves its own traders short.
      - Added a PDA remark from a nearby stalker when a trader runs short of a staple.
    Trade
      - Changed stalkers to buy usable rounds instead of the cheapest damaged ammo.
      - Changed stalkers to restock food, drink and anti-rad at traders, and veterans also buy pills, tools and repair parts.
      - Fixed NPC sales handing gear to the trader. A sold item is released.

  General
    - Fixed an off-map squad that timed out leaving its members behind in the world.
    - Added Russian text for the MCM reset confirmations.

1.8.2
  A squad change sensor, A-Life Rate and Ratio, and fixes from Muratovnik
    A squad event now fires when a squad moves, crosses a level or goes online, and A-Life Rate sets how many fire per minute.
    A-Life Ratio splits that rate between your map and the other maps.
    Other things you will notice. Alphas, mutation caps, gossip and massacre reactions are fixed, the overlay shows sections per stage, and stalkers restock more often.

  Framework
    - Changed the squad update to fire only when a squad really changes, a move to another smart, a level crossing or going online or offline.
      A-Life Rate produces that many squad events per minute across the Zone, and A-Life Ratio splits them between your map and the rest. It replaces a stream of throttled vanilla updates.
    - Added a vanilla A-Life fix that keeps a smart's squad count right when a squad relocates, and off-map travellers now settle at their destination.

  Creatures
    - Fixed the kill counts of despawned NPCs passing to new entities and promoting mutants to alpha. Diagnosed by Muratovnik.

  Territory
    - Fixed mutation caps lowered in MCM not applying to an existing save. A restore trims to the cap. PR by Muratovnik.

  Economy
    Loot claim
      - Fixed enemies voicing the leave-a-kill remark. Only neutral and friendly stalkers do.
      - Fixed error spam when the loot claim read a corpse with no spine bone.

  News
    - Fixed the radio gossiping already broadcast events again after a reload or a level change. Diagnosed by Muratovnik.

  Causes
    Reactions
      - Fixed massacre and base attack reactions held back during the heavy combat that triggers them. Diagnosed by Muratovnik.
      - Changed a heal by the player to draw enemy hunts or ally aid for any medical item. Diagnosed by Muratovnik.
    Needs
      - Changed the Supply need to come due sooner by default, and stalkers restock twice as often.

  Development
    - Changed the statistics overlay to read as a ledger, with incoming, denied, evaluated and outcome sections and rates over the last minute.
    - Added a compatibility status for the xlibs, xray-monolith and AOEngine versions, with a clear pass or fail.
    - Fixed an outdated xlibs crashing AlifePlus on load. The dependency check shows the update message.

1.8.1
  A save repair for old loot ownership data
    A save that carries loot ownership data from before 1.8.0 repairs itself on load.

  - Fixed a save from before 1.8.0 carrying loot ownership rows the new loot claim could not read. They are dropped on load.

1.8.0
  The faction market, symmetric chase and kill ownership, and fair corpse looting
    Economy splits into pages. A faction's hub traders briefly stock what its stalkers sold, and the loot ownership of 1.7.7 now holds in every direction.
    Chases now follow the target's live position for you and for NPCs alike, and a looting NPC keeps a fair share of a body.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers voice trader news on the PDA, a map where you are the only enemy no longer aims every reaction at you, and squads leave a full campfire.

  Economy
    Market
      - Added the Market. A faction's hub traders briefly stock a few items its stalkers recently sold, gated to your rank, priced at a premium and cleared after a short window.
        It works only with real items that stalkers sold through trade after looting them or carrying them in their loadouts.
      - Added PDA chatter. A nearby stalker remarks when his faction's trader restocks something notable.
    Loot claim
      - Added kill ownership in every direction. Your kills are reserved from NPCs, an NPC's from you, and NPCs no longer strip each other's kills.
        The claim covers the killer's whole squad, and the body stays held while the squad stands over it. Each side has its own switch, radius and claim time.
    Loot policy
      - Added the loot policy. A looting NPC keeps ammo for his own weapon and a capped share of each supply, and the rest is destroyed.
        Bodies you reach later still hold their gear, and loot blocker addons are no longer needed.
      - Added remarks from NPCs who leave a kill for you or for another squad.
    Trade
      - Changed loot, trade and stash to share the same item policies.

  Framework
    - Added Reactions per causer. Each instigator triggers only so many reactions per game hour, and a map where you are the only enemy no longer aims every reaction at you.

  Consequences
    - Changed chases to follow the target's live position, the same for you and for NPCs. A chase ends when the target dies, leaves the map or stops being hostile.
      It pauses while the target sits in a base or a surge is on.
    - Changed squads at a full base campfire to move on and find room elsewhere, and squads that scatter off a fire or stand on an empty slot are released.

1.7.9
  Interaction Dot Marks compatibility for the loot claim
    The NPC kill block now holds against Interaction Dot Marks.

  - Fixed Interaction Dot Marks opening, taking all from and auto-looting an NPC's claimed kill.

1.7.8
  Loot ownership toggles, a full open block, and faction and companion rules
    An NPC's claimed kill no longer opens at all, and the reserve and the block have separate toggles.

  Economy
    - Changed an NPC's claimed kill to stay closed. It used to block only the item takes, and auto-loot through the loot window is stopped with it.
    - Changed loot ownership into 2 toggles, reserve your kills and block looting NPC kills.
    - Changed an enemy faction's kill to stay open to you. Only the claims of neutral and friendly stalkers hold.
    - Changed the body of your own companion to stay yours to recover.
    - Changed the claim warning to vary across several lines.
    - Improved corpse loot ownership on a save load or a level change.

1.7.7
  Loot ownership, a trade profit cap, wider off-map travel and AOEngine support
    Economy is a new tab. Your kills are reserved from NPC looters nearby, and an NPC's kill stays closed while its killer is close.
    Other things you will notice. Trade caps an NPC's profit, veteran-led squads travel off-map, and AlifePlus runs on AOEngine.

  Economy
    - Added loot ownership both ways, with its radius under Economy.
    - Added Trade profit cap, the net rubles an NPC gains per trade at any rank.
    - Changed trade and stash to keep smoke grenades out of NPC item flow. A smoke grenade an NPC throws crashes the game on current exes.

  World
    Off-map
      - Changed off-map travel to include veteran-led squads. Only master-led squads used to make the trip.

  Causes
    Reactions
      - Fixed massacre investigations firing when a mutant pack wipes a stalker squad.

  Compatibility
    - Added AOEngine support.

1.7.6
  An off-map crash guard, an MCM reset fix and a save repair
    Off-map dispatch survives a squad whose class binding is broken, and the MCM reset buttons no longer crash.

  - Fixed off-map dispatch crashing on a squad whose class binding is broken.
  - Fixed Reset ALL to Defaults and Reset ALL to Stateless Defaults crashing on some exes.
  - Fixed stale off-map tracking from earlier versions. A save repairs it on load.
  - Added a warning above the reset buttons to save or discard pending MCM changes first.

1.7.5
  The trade rework, off-map social visits, item-keeping arrivals and stateless reset
    Stalkers now trade like the player. They visit traders to sell their surplus and restock by rank, on a trade policy you can edit in DLTX.
    Added Social Off-map. Peaceful factions visit other maps for downtime, and arrivals at campfires and shelters leave carried items alone.
    Other things you will notice. Stash policy is editable, supply runs reach every trader, medic and mechanic, and quest items survive NPC trade.

  Economy
    Trade
      - Changed trade to run on arrival at a trader. An NPC sells his surplus and restocks ammo, grenades and consumables by rank, on Alundaio's buy and sell core.
        The policy is editable per rank in a DLTX config, and addon items take their category on their own, so AI medkits, AP rounds and GAMMA ammo all work.
      - Changed rookies to carry the basics and veterans premium ammo, grenades and larger stocks, with a profit cap per rank. Sales come first and fund the restock.

  Causes
    Needs
      - Changed arrivals at campfires, shelters and outposts to leave carried items alone.
      - Added Social Off-map. Peaceful sociable factions travel to another map for downtime, and Ecologists, Loners and Clear Sky turn up at bases like the Cordon farm and Yantar.
      - Changed Supply Trader Off-map to peaceful greedy factions only. Outlaws stay in their territory.
      - Changed supply runs to reach every trader, medic and mechanic in the Zone, the vanilla mechanics and quest NPCs included.
    Opportunities
      - Changed the stash policy to a DLTX config. Ammo goes to the squad member whose gun takes it, the best extras by cost come after, and a stash with a quest item is skipped.

  Development
    - Added Reset ALL to Stateless Defaults and the Social Off-map pages.
    - Removed the cash cap, the stash loot and fill sliders and the arrive action toggles.
    - Fixed Reset ALL to Defaults needing a second click.

  Compatibility
    - Changed NPC trade and stash deposits to leave quest items, companion gifts and weapons the player strapped alone.

  Performance
    - Improved world scan performance for the creatures, chests and smarts on your level.

1.7.1
  A load-time stutter fix for the world scan caches
    A save with a large A-Life population loads without a long frame drop.

  - Fixed a save load dropping the frame rate for several seconds on a large A-Life population.
  - Changed the standalone NPC cache to index stalkers only, which shrinks the queue from the whole A-Life pool to the real stalker population.

1.7.0
  The stalker trade economy, faster world scans, reactive preemption and Area Swarm
    Supply Trader now trades. Stalkers at a supply trader sell their loot and buy ammo for the guns they carry, on the trade rules the player uses.
    World scans run on per-level caches, and a reaction can now pull a squad off a routine trip.
    Other things you will notice. Area Swarm has a page, the area mutators start on, squads weigh a trip's tactics, and alphas fight at vanilla strength again.

  Territory
    - Added the Area Swarm page.
    - Changed Conquest, Swarm and Infest to start on, with the same per-level cap. An upgrade clears the held areas once, and live dispatch fills them again.
    - Removed the Alpha and Stalker Rank pages. Alphas and veteran stalkers take vanilla damage and drop vanilla loot, and alpha promotion stays.

  Causes
    Needs
      - Added trade at the supply trader. A squad sells loot for money and buys ammo for its pistols and rifles, PDAs, medkits, bandages and grenades from a keep list.
        Only smarts with a curated trader, medic or mechanic count, a veteran or higher buys grenades, and a cash cap sends the excess back. Built on Alundaio and Tronex's offline trade.
      - Changed arrivals to use what the need asks for. Hunger eats food and drink, cooked mutant meat included, healing uses medical items, and rest, social and outpost visits use anti-rad.
      - Changed the Supply and Job needs to weigh more. Trade and outpost trips come before campfires and shelters when several needs are due.
      - Removed Social Off-base.
    Opportunities
      - Changed Stash Loot to skip a stash that holds a crafting item, and to take only items on the keep list otherwise.
      - Changed Stash Fill to deposit only the squad's surplus above the keep floor. AlifePlus no longer spawns items into a stash.
      - Changed stash trips to fire at any smart outside a base, and while the squad sits at its faction's base.

  Consequences
    - Changed reactions to take squads off an on-map need, an instinct or a stash ambush. Squads on a territory take, a stash run, an off-map trip or a reaction carry on.
    - Added tactical scoring for radiant trips. A trip that leaves the source smart undefended by its faction, or heads where another scripted squad is going, scores lower and is rejected more often.
    - Changed a reaction to fire at most 2 consequences.
    - Fixed hostility going stale on long dispatches, and chasers following you after their faction turned friendly.
    - Fixed the smart roster missing AlifePlus squad moves. Integrator mods get a squad enters smart and a squad leaves smart callback.

  News
    - Changed the news to come half as often by default.

  Performance
    - Improved world scan performance with per-level caches that refresh across frames.
    - Changed the radiant scan budget to count per generator, spent only when a cause scans the world.

1.6.0
  Off-map travel, the news rework and faction relation fixes
    World is a new tab. Squads travel to a neighboring map for supply, scouting or a social visit, as far as your story progress allows.
    The news reads the activity record, and the PDA marker shows the action, the subject and the target.
    Other things you will notice. Robbers and avengers read a target's true faction, and the base checks look at the squad's faction.

  World
    Off-map
      - Added off-map travel. Squads go to a neighboring map for supply, scouting or a social visit, and Army, Monolith and the Zombified stay home.
        Reach increases with Yantar X-16, the Brain Scorcher and a master-rank commander, and a cap per source map limits the trips.
        Squads return home after a stay, and a squad stuck off-map is released once offline. Story, task, companion and Warfare squads are spared.
      - Fixed the off-map lifecycle dropping a squad's script mid-transit and queuing a return from a place it never visited.

  News
    - Changed the composer to read the activity record.
    - Changed the PDA marker to show the action, the consequence, the subject, the target smart with its level and the dispatch time.
    - Removed the News Chance slider.

  Consequences
    - Fixed Harvest Rob and Squadkill Revenge reading the target's disguise in place of his true community.
    - Fixed Wounded, Stash, Massacre, Squadkill and Basekill checking any base where they should check a base of the squad's faction.
    - Fixed swarms going to smarts whose props reject their species.
    - Fixed peer causes having a fixed first pick.
    - Fixed alpha loot stacking several pelts on one kill.

  Development
    - Added Teleport to squad on the right-click menu of an AlifePlus map marker, gated by the debug markers toggle.
    - Changed the map markers toggle and the per-consequence cap to apply mid-session.
    - Changed the A-Life interval default to a longer one, and the mutator settings reset to defaults on the first load.

  Modder API
    - Added calls for a squad's home level and to publish and read activity records, with record fields as localization keys.
    - Changed the Warfare shim to pass the activity record to erepb's Warfare A-Life Overhaul.

1.5.5
  Animated destinations, Mutant Swarm, Massacre Loot, the day and night split and the modder API
    Squads now go only to smart terrains with animation jobs, and a squad whose slot is taken on the way returns to the simulation.
    Added Mutant Swarm, Massacre Loot and slumber by species. Mutants swarm empty smarts, outlaws loot massacres, and mutants sleep by kind, in their territory, a lair or a surge shelter.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers work by day and sleep at night, and each faction has a stash role. The MCM regroups its causes, and the Russian MCM matches the English.

  Causes
    - Changed the radiant pipeline to run the rules and the scan at the cause, and to give every squad a fair turn. Each squad picks the action that fits its faction, species, personality and hour.
    - Changed the cause budgets to count per category, Reactions, Needs, Instincts and Opportunities, so a busy category cannot starve another.
    - Changed each cause attempt to pick one specific action, a campfire halt, a lair retreat, a stash fill or a surge shelter, for more variety per drive.
    - Changed work to happen by day and sleep and shelter by night, with eating, healing, rest and social at any hour. Mutants follow their species' cycle, and nocturnal species invert it.
    - Changed the destinations to smart terrains with real animation jobs. A squad whose slot is taken between dispatch and arrival returns to the simulation.
    - Changed stash work by alignment. Outlaws ambush, Loners, Clear Sky, Freedom and Mercenaries loot, and Duty, the Military, Monolith, ISG and Ecologists fill.
    - Changed the stash and area cooldowns to game-hour thresholds per cause, and infestation joins Conquer and Swarm in the Area family.
    - Changed the personality floor lower, and faction differences widen.
    - Changed newly tracked squads to act on the first tick after a load.
    - Added over 100 smaller changes to routing, personality, alignment and squad choices.

  Consequences
    - Added Mutant Swarm. Feral, predator and aberrant squads claim empty smart terrains next to the original spawns.
    - Added Massacre Loot. Bandits, renegades and Greh strip massacre sites for weapons and gear.
    - Added slumber by species. Cowardly mutants bed down in their territory, feral and predator mutants retreat to lairs, and aberrant and predator mutants seek a surge shelter.
    - Changed Massacre Scavenge to the cowardly mutants and Wounded Hunt to predator and aberrant mutants.
    - Changed Stash Ambush to presence only, and Stash Fill to roll its items on arrival.
    - Changed a held conquest to turn over more often.
    - Removed Squadkill Flee, which the engine does not support well.
    - Fixed Mutant Swarm not publishing, and Squadkill Revenge missing NPC-vs-NPC kills.
    - Fixed Alpha Kill reacting to story NPCs, traders and named characters.
    - Fixed scripted squads stuck when a destination's animation conditions flipped before arrival, and squads with free job slots ejected on arrival.
    - Fixed peaceful trips and stash trips ending at a hostile faction's smart.
    - Fixed Harvest Haunt and Wounded Hunt sending mutant squads with a broken commander.

  News
    - Added a News Chance slider.
    - Changed the templates to one set per consequence. Any speaker can now voice any template.
    - Changed the PDA marker to show the action, the consequence and the subject.
    - Fixed PDA markers missing for massacre, basekill, harvest haunt and wounded squads.
    - Fixed capitalized mutant and faction names in the news, and zombified squads using human templates.

  MCM
    - Changed the causes to a page each for Reactions, Opportunities, Needs and Instincts, each read as Cause, Description and Rules in plain English.
    - Added the per-category budgets, the stash and area toggles and thresholds, the Mutators tab, a Stash Ambush minimum and a Massacre Loot section.
    - Removed the master toggles, the drive toggles and the personality sliders. One global clamp applies to every roll.

  Compatibility
    - Added a save migration that releases scripted squads whose arrival consequence no longer exists.
    - Added a shim for erepb's GAMMA fork of Warfare A-Life Overhaul.

  Modder API
    - Added the public modder API, documented in the integration guide, for squad ownership, dispatch, localized phrases, foreign causes and consequences, and cleanup.
    - Added the ACTION and CAUSE_CATEGORY enums.
    - Removed the activity record API.

  Localization
    - Added the Massacre Loot templates and a Russian MCM at parity with the English. Stalker_Boss translates Russian and gwalls copyedits English.

1.5.0
  PDA news, mutant infestation, additive conquest and the first modder API
    News is a new tab. A stalker on your frequency relays what squads do as radio chatter, picked by how much it matters and how close he was.
    Added infestation. A mutant alpha turns a smart into a single-species nest, and a conquest adds the winner's spawns beside the originals.
    Other things you will notice. Personality follows the lore more closely, the PDA marker names both sides, and every text ships in English and Russian.

  News
    - Added the PDA news. The framework records every cause and consequence, and a speaker who took part, saw it or stood near relays it as hearsay, a witness, a survivor, a tracker or a named report.
      It runs on the vanilla news queue, respects emissions, psi storms, PDA charge and faction channels, and reaches your faction, your allies or the whole world.

  Consequences
    - Added mutant infestation. Feral, predator and aberrant alphas claim smart terrains as nests, and the infesting species replaces the original spawns.
    - Changed territory conquest to add the winner's spawns beside the originals, which leaves a mixed zone as vanilla does.
    - Changed stash fill and every stash cause to skip bases.
    - Changed personality values and the default ceiling to follow the lore.
    - Fixed Squadkill Revenge chasing you after your own-faction kills drifted your relation hostile.

  MCM
    - Added the News tab, the infest instinct settings and the infestation mutator settings.
    - Removed the PDA chance sliders per consequence.

  Development
    - Changed the PDA map marker to a multi-line label with the action, the subject and the other side.
    - Added spawn tracing for every squad that conquest or infestation spawns.

  Modder API
    - Added the activity record API, localized consequence captions in English and Russian, and spawn injection beside or in place of a smart's spawns.

1.4.0
  Mutant instincts, the day and night cycle, the food chain and range-based perception
    Added mutant instincts beside the stalker needs. Mutants scatter, feed, sleep, explore and gather, and each group avoids the ones above it in the food chain.
    Added the day and night cycle and range tiers. Stalkers work by day and rest at night, nocturnal mutants hunt in the dark, and a cause reaches as far as a squad sees, radios or smells.
    Other things you will notice. Mutants hunt an alpha's killer, artefact pickups draw reactions, and a statistics overlay shows the pipeline.

  Causes
    - Added mutant instincts, scatter, feed, sleep, explore and socialize, scored by how long each drive has gone unmet, beside the stalker needs.
    - Changed mutant personality and alignment to follow GSC's monster design, with species detection through xlibs.
    - Added the food chain. Cowardly mutants avoid feral, predator and aberrant ones, feral avoid predator and aberrant, and predators avoid aberrant.
    - Added the day and night cycle. Stalkers work by day and rest at night, and bloodsuckers, lurkers, chimeras, zombies and fractures hunt at night and retreat at dawn.
    - Added range-based perception. Each cause reaches as far as the squad sees, radios or smells, measured on smart terrain spacing across the levels.
    - Changed the death of an alpha to send its species on the level after the killer.
    - Added artefact pickup reactions. Outlaws chase the taker, and aberrant mutants converge on the site.
    - Changed decay and cooldown timers to game time.

  Framework
    - Changed the pipeline to filter ineligible squads before the budget, and to try the next cause at once when one is rejected.
    - Added squad ownership reassertion, dead squad cleanup and a block on invalid cause and consequence pairs.

  Development
    - Added the statistics overlay, live pipeline rates, blockers and counts, at a position set in MCM.
    - Changed the map markers to blue icons that linger after the trip ends, then fade.

  Modder API
    - Added the activity record API and PDA marker descriptions, and register_owner supports an override.

  Compatibility
    - Removed the modded exes requirement. AlifePlus runs on vanilla Anomaly 1.5.3, the demonized exes and AOEngine, tested with GAMMA, EFP and Zona.

1.3.6
  A save migration hotfix
    A save from an earlier version releases and rebuilds its old scripted squad entries on load.

  - Fixed old scripted squad entries in a save. They are released and rebuilt on load.

1.3.5
  Alignment, alpha mutants, chained reactions and combat mutators
    Added alignment, GSC's moral axis of principled, self-serving, unprincipled and outlaw, and mutants hold territory, avenge their dead and hunt the wounded.
    A mutant that racks up kills becomes an alpha, and a single event now draws several independent responses.
    Other things you will notice. Squads stay at a destination long enough for camp jobs to play out, and the readme ships in Russian.

  Causes
    - Added the alignment system on GSC's moral axis. The Military holds its ground, Ecologists leave conquest to others and renegades skip investigations.
    - Added mutant territorial behavior. Mutants conquer territory, avenge their dead and hunt wounded stalkers by their personality.
    - Changed reactions to chain. A squad wipe fires both revenge and retreat, a medkit use draws predators and sends allies to help, and a massacre draws scavengers and investigators.
    - Changed the personality chances narrower, so factions act true to their identity more often.
    - Removed stalker elites and the elite kill bounty. X-Ray tracks a stalker's progress through his rank.

  Consequences
    - Added alpha mutants. A mutant that racks up kills hits harder, takes more punishment, never flees and drops bonus loot of its species, scaling with its kill level.
    - Added alpha kill retaliation. Killing an alpha sends its species after the killer.
    - Added squad death responses by species. Predators and territorial packs avenge their members, and herbivores and weak mobs scatter.
    - Changed squads to stay at a destination long enough for camp jobs, patrols and sleep to play out. Every squad used to leave after a few minutes.
    - Fixed a crash on fast travel when a scripted squad died offline and X-Ray recycled its id.

  Mutators
    - Added the Mutators section, with toggles for the alpha and stalker combat modifiers. An alpha's hit power scales with its kill level, and a veteran stalker's with his rank.

  Localization
    - Added the full Russian readme, and the Russian MCM matches the English.

1.3.0
  Personality, mutant conquest, territory decay and the ownership registry
    Every stalker and mutant faction now has a personality, and its traits pick the consequences it takes.
    Mutants now conquer territory, conquered ground decays when nobody holds it, and other A-Life mods can mark the squads they own.
    Other things you will notice. Save data cleans up on an upgrade, arrivals are detected faster, and the post-arrival wait follows game time.

  Causes
    - Added personality profiles for every stalker and mutant faction, whose traits pick the consequence. Hunger and sleep use survival, money greed, jobs territory and perception, social relation.
    - Added a cooldown per smart for the area cause, so a location cannot trigger conquest again and again.
    - Changed the per-consequence budget tighter, so one consequence cannot dominate a session.
    - Removed the per-consequence chance sliders. The personality system replaces them.

  Consequences
    - Added territory decay. A conquered area decays after a set number of game hours unless it is taken again.
    - Added a persistent PDA marker for an elite's squad until it dies.
    - Changed the post-arrival wait to game time, which advances in a time skip and survives a save.
    - Changed the arrival scan to detect an arrival faster.
    - Changed the stash consequences to the config pattern the needs use.
    - Removed job_worship and job_exercise.
    - Fixed the area conquest toggle having no effect on smarts already conquered.
    - Fixed radiant causes not firing in the first session after a game start, and needs thresholds breaking on a young save.

  Modder API
    - Added the squad ownership registry. An A-Life mod registers a filter, and AlifePlus skips the squads it owns. Warfare and BAO register through legacy proxies.
    - Added the integration API for custom causes and consequences.
    - Fixed the Warfare and BAO filters claiming squads without the expected field.

  Compatibility
    - Added save data cleanup on an upgrade. Orphaned squads are released and stale keys removed.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to the new version.

  Performance
    - Improved pipeline performance. The chance rolls are gone, the protection gate allocates nothing below DEBUG, and the producer makes fewer engine calls.

1.2.3
  The radiant and reactive split, NPC protection and the PDA rebuild
    The pipeline splits world changes from combat events, each rate-limited apart, and a global cooldown stops bursts in busy areas.
    Protected NPCs go through a single check at every layer, and PDA messages come from stalkers already in the world.
    Other things you will notice. Map markers have their own toggle, territory changes hands only on arrival, and squads stop oscillating between nearby spots.

  Framework
    - Added the radiant and reactive split, with each rate-limited on its own.
    - Added a global radiant cooldown against consequence bursts in busy areas.
    - Changed consequence chances to a pseudo-random distribution.

  Consequences
    - Fixed territory changing hands before the conquering squad arrived.
    - Fixed stashes filled while not empty, and mutant squads triggering stalker stash events.
    - Fixed squads oscillating between nearby locations.
    - Fixed revenge rolling against factions that are not enemies, and elite hunters ignoring the protection list.

  Compatibility
    - Changed NPC protection to one check for permanent squads, active roles, task targets and squads another mod scripts, applied at the producer, the search and the tracker.

  News
    - Changed the PDA sender to follow the vanilla news manager, friendly factions only, from the stalkers already online.
    - Added a toggle for the map markers apart from debug tracing.

  Development
    - Added the mod and xlibs versions at startup, and the Russian MCM reads in windows-1251 again.
    - Fixed timed events with the demonized time events addon and the major modpacks.

