1.2.0
  Needs with item use, area conquest options, stash protection and shelter routing
    Named NPCs, traders, quest givers and guards stay out of AlifePlus, and squads on another mission are skipped.
    Squads walk or rush per consequence, skip stashes with essential items, and seek a campfire when no indoor shelter is near.
    Other things you will notice. Needs back off after a failed search, heal and shelter head to surge shelters, and squads at a full location complete their action and leave.

  Causes
    - Added stash fill at bases, while ambush and loot stay blocked there.
    - Changed area conquest to target enemy or unclaimed territory only, and revenge and elite hunters to skip friendly factions.
    - Changed a need that cannot find a destination to back off and give other needs a turn.
    - Changed heal and shelter to target surge shelters, and heal, shelter and social to accept any location that is not hostile.
    - Changed guard, worship and exercise to send squads to outposts and forward positions.

  Consequences
    - Added a walk or rush toggle per consequence.
    - Added stash protection. NPCs skip stashes with toolkits and essential items.
    - Added an area conquest toggle that keeps the squad movement without changing smart ownership.
    - Added Shelter Outdoor. Squads seek a campfire when no indoor shelter is near.
    - Changed squads at a full location to complete their action and return to the simulation.

  Compatibility
    - Fixed named NPCs, traders, quest givers and guards taking part, and squads on a mission being taken over.
    - Fixed squads responding to their own events.

  Stability
    - Fixed the elite kill PDA always using the mutant template, consequence handlers duplicating across a save and load, and artefact drops looping harvest chasers.
    - Changed squad tracking to game time, which survives sleep and time acceleration.

1.2.0-RC1
  The Needs system, the radiant and reactive split, PDA messages and the manifesto
    Stalkers now act on needs of their own, hunger, sleep, rest, heal, shelter, money, supply, job and social, beyond the events they react to.
    Other things you will notice. PDA messages tell stalkers from mutants, the MCM has a reset button, and the manifesto explains the design.

  Needs
    - Added 9 needs with per-need MCM controls, a night gate, a faction-aware destination filter and per-squad save data.
    - Added arrival actions. NPCs use real inventory items or trade artefacts for supplies.

  Framework
    - Added the radiant and reactive split with separate token buckets, so reactive events no longer starve.

  News
    - Added PDA message variants for each category, with stalkers and mutants told apart.

  MCM
    - Added a reset button and Russian text.

  Fixed
    - Fixed wounded_help matching the wrong faction, and supply_trader giving items for free. It now takes an artefact.

